# Environmental Consultant / Project Manager
Salary
Up to £35,000
Location
Bridgend, UK
*This is a {Advertised Permanent / Temporary}, {Advertised Full Time / Part Time} vacancy that will close in a month at 23:59 BST.*
**The Vacancy**
**RSK Raw** part of the RSK Group have an exciting new opportunity for an **Environmental Consultant/Project manager** to join our team in **Bridgend, UK.**
RSK RAW offers multi-disciplinary environmental protection and risk reduction services to a wide range of industries and clients across the UK, and are specialists in the provision of spill response, contamination investigation and remediation projects.
**Key Responsibilities:**
* Managing and delivering rapid response to environmental incidents in a variety of urban and rural settings;
* Pro-active assessment of pollution risks to the environment and the application of a variety of techniques for containing and recovering oils or other contaminants of concern;
* Maintaining accurate site notes, and excellent time management, organisational and communication skills at all times;
* Undertaking Phase I and Phase II site investigations;
* Carrying out desk-based research;
* Preparing site plans;
* Organising, undertaking, and supervising site works;
* Procuring and managing subcontractors for allocated projects, ensuring control of financial and health and safety matters;
* Preparing cost proposals / tenders;
* Preparing factual and interpretative reports;
* Preparing Health and Safety documentation, including method statements, risk assessments and site records;
* Adherence to RSK Raw management systems, including site specific and point of work health & safety risk assessments and method statements;
* Financial control of allocated projects including project driven invoicing, issuing of purchase orders, and chasing payment on outstanding and overdue invoices;
* Accountable for management and performance of projects and continued delivery of a high quality service, providing clear, commercially focused solutions;
* Pro-active client management, maintaining good communication throughout the lifecycle of a project, being aware of the client's needs and providing regular progress reports and confirming any variances as they arise.
**Additional information:**
* We operate a 24/7 spill response service for our clients. As such, you may be required to work out of normal operating hours, for which you will be compensated.
* Although the role is regionally focussed, there may sometimes be a need for travel and staying away from home to cover the needs of the business throughout England, Scotland, and Wales.
* There are opportunities available for collaborative working with other businesses within the RSK Group.
**Qualifications/Experience:**
* At least 3 years' relevant industry experience;
* Project management experience (desirable);
* A degree level qualification in a science / environment / land related subject;
* Associate membership of a professional body (desirable);
* Flexible attitude to work;
* Enthusiasm and drive to deliver the requirements of this role;
* The ability to work as an effective member of a team and on your own initiative;
* Excellent communication, organisational and problem-solving skills;
* CSCS card;
* Full UK / EC driving licence (essential).
**Salary and Benefits:**
* Salary Up to £35,000 depending on experience
* Contributory pension scheme
* A flexible benefits programme, including the option to buy additional holidays and private healthcare
* Regular training and career development
**The RSK Group are an equal opportunity employer**
