# # **About Us**
**Wellington Management** offers comprehensive investment management capabilities that span nearly all segments of the global capital markets. Our investment solutions, tailored to the unique return and risk objectives of institutional clients in more than 60 countries, draw on a robust body of proprietary research and a collaborative culture that encourages independent thought and healthy debate. As a private partnership, we believe our ownership structure fosters a long-term view that aligns our perspectives with those of our clients.
# # About the Role
**The Position**
We are currently seeking to recruit an experienced Business Development Manager to join the European Client Group, and to lead the firm’s business development activities with Institutional & Wealth prospects and clients in the Netherlands. This individual will play an important strategic role in driving growth across Wellington’s full product suite with pension funds, public institutions, wealth intermediaries, and insurance companies in the market. The role will either be situated in the Netherlands, or in London, or in another Wellington European hub.
**Responsibilities**
Core Responsibilities will include:
\* Developing and executing the firm’s sales strategy with Institutional, Wealth and Consultant prospects and clients in the Netherlands;
\* Driving growth across the firm’s range of investment strategies, in line with business priorities;
\* Developing successful long term relationship with strategic partners, in partnership with Relationship Management colleagues;
\* Contributing to the development of wider industry relationships;
\* Partnering closely with Marketing and PR colleagues to ensure that local marketing and sales strategies are closely aligned, and contributing to the continued growth in brand awareness;
\* Providing guidance and direction to Relationship Analysts;
\* Ensuring compliance with evolving regulatory requirements.
**Qualifications**
The successful candidate is likely to:
\* Have 10+ years of relevant industry experience, including experience of leading Institutional sales activities in the Dutch market;
\* Have a demonstrable track record of successfully developing and managing a network of Institutional & Wealth client relationships;
\* Have a comprehensive understanding of competitors, products, key market trends, and industry developments;
\* Demonstrate an in-depth knowledge of financial markets and investment strategies, and an ability to influence through a content-led, consultative sales approach;
\* Be action orientated, accountable, committed, driven and self-motivated, with excellent communication and team working skills;
\* Have the ability to prioritise, focus, eliminate roadblocks and execute a sales strategy in a timely manner;
\* Demonstrate a high level of integrity and trust, and a client centric focus;
\* Have a strong academic background, including an undergraduate degree. A relevant professional qualification (e.g. CFA) would be viewed favourably;
\* Be fluent in English and Dutch.
Please note that we are only able to respond to successful applicants.
Not sure you meet 100% of our qualifications? That’s ok. If you believe that you could excel in this role, we encourage you to apply and welcome a chance to review your background. We are dedicated to building and maintaining a diversified workforce and considering a broad array of candidates with a variety of skill, workplace experiences, and backgrounds.
